IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g4-conflict`

-- g4-tests-conflict.l4: tests for g4-conflict.l4 (s.29).  Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of s.29 (inputs/law.wiki lines 229-242)
-- before the module was run: see work/g4/expectations.md.  Each #ASSERT is one scenario; each #TRACE carries its expected outcome in the
-- `-- EXPECT` comment above it.

§ `Tests for section 29`

§§ `The first definition: family member`

-- Each relation the definition lists is a family member; a relation it does not list is not.  (Step-relations are included in each listed kind.)
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a spouse of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of a parent of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a spouse of a child of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a brother or sister of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of a brother or sister of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a brother-in-law or sister-in-law of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `an uncle or aunt of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a child of an uncle or aunt of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a parent of a spouse of the member`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a grandchild of the member`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.1 — the relation is that of a family member` `a relation section 29(a) does not list`

§§ `The third definition: handling`

#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `taking a decision on the matter` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `raising the subject for discussion` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `being present at the discussion` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `taking part in the discussion or in the vote` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `engaging with the subject outside the discussion` FALSE
-- "לרבות": the list is open; a way it does not list is handling only by judgement (an input).
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `another way of dealing with the matter` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.3 — the way of dealing with the matter is handling` `another way of dealing with the matter` FALSE

§§ `The fifth definition: relative`

-- Fields: kinship | the member has an interest in the party's financial position | corporation | member interested party | family member interested party
--         | a category-(2) person interested party | body | member manages | family member manages | a category-(2) person manages.
`a spouse`                                                MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a spouse of the member`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a stranger in whose finances the member has an interest` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a stranger with nothing`                                 MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a corporation the member is an interested party in`      MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a corporation a family member is an interested party in` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a corporation a category-(2) person is an interested party in` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a corporation nobody connected is an interested party in` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`something that is no corporation, though the member is said to be an interested party` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a body the member manages`                                MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`a body a family member manages`                           MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`a body a category-(2) person manages`                     MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a body only a stranger manages`                           MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`something that is no body, though the member is said to manage it` MEANS `Party in relation to a member of the Council` OF `a relation section 29(a) does not list`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(1) — the party is a family member of the member` `a spouse`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a spouse`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(2) — the member has an interest in the financial position of the party` `a stranger in whose finances the member has an interest`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a stranger in whose finances the member has an interest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5(1) — the party is a family member of the member` `a stranger in whose finances the member has an interest`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a stranger with nothing`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(3) — the party is a corporation in which the member, a family member or a person of category (2) is an interested party` `a corporation the member is an interested party in`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a corporation the member is an interested party in`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(3) — the party is a corporation in which the member, a family member or a person of category (2) is an interested party` `a corporation a family member is an interested party in`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(3) — the party is a corporation in which the member, a family member or a person of category (2) is an interested party` `a corporation a category-(2) person is an interested party in`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5(3) — the party is a corporation in which the member, a family member or a person of category (2) is an interested party` `a corporation nobody connected is an interested party in`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a corporation nobody connected is an interested party in`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `something that is no corporation, though the member is said to be an interested party`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(4) — the party is a body that the member, a family member or a person of category (2) manages or is responsibly employed in` `a body the member manages`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a body the member manages`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(4) — the party is a body that the member, a family member or a person of category (2) manages or is responsibly employed in` `a body a family member manages`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.5(4) — the party is a body that the member, a family member or a person of category (2) manages or is responsibly employed in` `a body a category-(2) person manages`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5(4) — the party is a body that the member, a family member or a person of category (2) manages or is responsibly employed in` `a body only a stranger manages`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `a body only a stranger manages`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.5 — the party is a relative of the member` `something that is no body, though the member is said to manage it`

§§ `The fourth definition and section 29(e): a conflict of interest`

-- Interests.  Fields: whose interest | the kind | it conflicts with the performance of the function | it is related to the Council's functions.
`the member's own personal interest, conflicting`            MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `a personal interest of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE
`the member's own personal interest, not conflicting`        MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `a personal interest of the holder`, FALSE, FALSE
`the member's own other role, conflicting`                   MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `another role of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE
`a spouse's personal interest, conflicting`                  MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF (`someone else as holder` `a spouse`), `a personal interest of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE
`a spouse's personal interest, not conflicting`              MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF (`someone else as holder` `a spouse`), `a personal interest of the holder`, FALSE, FALSE
`a stranger's personal interest, conflicting`                MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF (`someone else as holder` `a stranger with nothing`), `a personal interest of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE
`the other role of a corporation the member is an interested party in, conflicting` MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF (`someone else as holder` `a corporation the member is an interested party in`), `another role of the holder`, TRUE, FALSE
`the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting` MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `the interest of the public the member represents, as a kind of interest`, TRUE, TRUE
`the public's interest, not related to the Council, conflicting` MEANS `Interest bearing on the member's function under section 29` OF `the member as holder`, `the interest of the public the member represents, as a kind of interest`, TRUE, FALSE

-- (e) does not apply to a member outside the seats 7 to 11 (the first input).
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the member's own personal interest, conflicting`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the member's own personal interest, not conflicting`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the member's own other role, conflicting`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `a spouse's personal interest, conflicting`
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `a spouse's personal interest, not conflicting`
-- An interest of someone who is not a relative cannot make the member's conflict.
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `a stranger's personal interest, conflicting`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the other role of a corporation the member is an interested party in, conflicting`
-- s.29(e): the public's interest, related to the Council's functions, is no conflict for a member of the seats 7 to 11 ...
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`
-- ... but is one for a member outside them, and when it is not related to the Council's functions.
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the public's interest, not related to the Council, conflicting`
-- "בשל כך בלבד" (for that reason alone): a seats-7-to-11 member with a personal interest that conflicts is still in conflict.
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest by the interest` `the member's own personal interest, conflicting`

-- The list.
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`, `the member's own personal interest, conflicting`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`, `the member's own personal interest, not conflicting`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `, is in a conflict of interest among the interests` EMPTY
#ASSERT `s 29(a) def.4, (e) — the member, who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `, is in a conflict of interest among the interests` (LIST `the public's interest, related to the Council, conflicting`)

§§ `Section 29(b): the bar on appointment and on service`

-- Both a regular conflict and one that prevents the main part of the function: neither alone.
#ASSERT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` TRUE `with the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` TRUE `with the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` FALSE `with the main part of the function prevented being` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 29(b) — the person is barred from the Council by regular conflicts of interest` FALSE `with the main part of the function prevented being` FALSE

-- Appointing a barred person is a breach; appointing anyone else is not.
-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(b): a person barred by regular conflicts of interest was appointed
#TRACE `s 29(b) — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person who would regularly be in a conflict of interest preventing the main part of the function` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to the Council` `the Minister` "dana" TRUE AT 4

-- EXPECT STANDING appoint a person to the Council
#TRACE `s 29(b) — the Minister must not appoint to the Council a person who would regularly be in a conflict of interest preventing the main part of the function` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `appoint a person to the Council` `the Minister` "dana" FALSE AT 4

-- A member who is barred and serves: a breach; one who is not barred: none.
-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(b): a member barred by regular conflicts of interest served
#TRACE `s 29(b) — a member who would regularly be in a conflict of interest preventing the main part of the function must not serve` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `serve as a member of the Council` `a Council member` TRUE AT 4

-- EXPECT STANDING serve as a member of the Council
#TRACE `s 29(b) — a member who would regularly be in a conflict of interest preventing the main part of the function must not serve` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `serve as a member of the Council` `a Council member` FALSE AT 4

§§ `Section 29(c): the bar on handling`

-- Fields of the act: the matter | the way of dealing | another way is handling | dealing puts the member in a conflict.
-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(c)
#TRACE `s 29(c) — a member must not handle a matter whose handling puts the member in a conflict of interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `deal with a matter in the member's function` `a Council member` "licence 42" `taking part in the discussion or in the vote` FALSE TRUE AT 6

-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(c)
#TRACE `s 29(c) — a member must not handle a matter whose handling puts the member in a conflict of interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `deal with a matter in the member's function` `a Council member` "licence 42" `being present at the discussion` FALSE TRUE AT 6

-- Handling a matter that does not put the member in a conflict is no breach.
-- EXPECT STANDING deal with a matter in the member's function
#TRACE `s 29(c) — a member must not handle a matter whose handling puts the member in a conflict of interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `deal with a matter in the member's function` `a Council member` "licence 43" `taking a decision on the matter` FALSE FALSE AT 6

-- A way of dealing that the definition does not list is handling only by judgement.
-- EXPECT STANDING deal with a matter in the member's function
#TRACE `s 29(c) — a member must not handle a matter whose handling puts the member in a conflict of interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `deal with a matter in the member's function` `a Council member` "licence 42" `another way of dealing with the matter` FALSE TRUE AT 6

-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(c)
#TRACE `s 29(c) — a member must not handle a matter whose handling puts the member in a conflict of interest` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `deal with a matter in the member's function` `a Council member` "licence 42" `another way of dealing with the matter` TRUE TRUE AT 6

§§ `Section 29(d): telling the chair, or the Minister`

-- A member who learned: telling the chair as soon as possible is fulfilment; telling late is a breach; no telling stands (no time is stated).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a member who learned of a possible conflict must tell the chair as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `tell the chair of the Council that the member may be in a conflict of interest` `a Council member` TRUE AT 2

-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(d): the chair was not told as soon as possible
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a member who learned of a possible conflict must tell the chair as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `tell the chair of the Council that the member may be in a conflict of interest` `a Council member` FALSE AT 90

-- EXPECT STANDING tell the chair of the Council that the member may be in a conflict of interest
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a member who learned of a possible conflict must tell the chair as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- A member who has not learned of anything owes nothing.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a member who learned of a possible conflict must tell the chair as soon as possible` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- The chair tells the Minister.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a chair who learned of a possible conflict must tell the Minister as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council chair` DOES `tell the Minister that the chair may be in a conflict of interest` `the Council chair` TRUE AT 2

-- EXPECT BREACH s 29(d): the Minister was not told as soon as possible
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a chair who learned of a possible conflict must tell the Minister as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Council chair` DOES `tell the Minister that the chair may be in a conflict of interest` `the Council chair` FALSE AT 90

-- EXPECT STANDING tell the Minister that the chair may be in a conflict of interest
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a chair who learned of a possible conflict must tell the Minister as soon as possible` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(d) — a chair who learned of a possible conflict must tell the Minister as soon as possible` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Section 29(e): taking the public's interests into account`

-- A member of seats 7 to 11, interests related to the Council's functions: the member MAY.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(e) — a member who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `may take into account the interests of the public the member represents, which are related to the Council's functions:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a Council member` DOES `take into account the interests of the public the member represents` `a Council member` AT 3

-- EXPECT STANDING take into account the interests of the public the member represents
#TRACE `s 29(e) — a member who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `may take into account the interests of the public the member represents, which are related to the Council's functions:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- A member outside the seats, or interests not related to the Council's functions: no such permission.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(e) — a member who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` FALSE `may take into account the interests of the public the member represents, which are related to the Council's functions:` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 29(e) — a member who sits in one of the seats 7 to 11:` TRUE `may take into account the interests of the public the member represents, which are related to the Council's functions:` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
